{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CdVkCox7G8iggpyF75HAz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants to be notified when a staging migration finishes or fails while they're away from their computer. They want their phone to buzz instead of having to check a terminal.\n\nLet me think about their options:\n\n1. **PushNotification tool** - This sends a notification to the user's phone directly through Claude Code\n2. **p9 skill** - The productive-wait primitive that can watch for a process/command completion and notify\n3. **Monitor tool** - Can stream events from background processes but doesn't notify phone\n4. **SendMessage** - Could send Slack/email notifications if configured\n5. **schedule/reminder** - Could set up a scheduled check\n\nLooking at the deferred tools available and the skills:\n- PushNotification would be perfect for this\n- The p9 skill mentions \"notify channels\" and can watch operations, then \"reports state + next action and pushes through the configured notify channels\"\n\nThe most direct approaches:\n1. Use `p9 wait-for <name> --cmd '<predicate>'` to monitor the migration and get notified\n2. Use PushNotification directly if there's a way to hook it to process completion\n3. Set up the monitoring with p9 which has built-in notification support\n\nThe user is asking \"what are my options and which one would you actually set up?\" - they want a recommendation.\n\nI should:\n1. Explain the main options\n2. Recommend which one is best\n3. Be ready to set it up if they approve\n\nThe p9 skill seems like the right tool here because:\n- It's designed for exactly this use case (watching external operations)\n- It has built-in \"configured notify channels\" \n- It handles both success and failure\n- It keeps the terminal clean with productive-wait (you work on other things while it watches)\n\nBut I need to understand what migration is running. They mentioned \"the staging migration\" but I don't know:\n- What command is running\n- How to check if it's done\n- What their notification preferences are\n\nI should recommend p9 as the best fit, then ask what command to monitor and where they'd prefer to receive alerts.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6938,"cache_read_input_tokens":17536,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6938},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"REDACTED","uuid":"3d86f704-197d-454e-a127-6c5ee960d4ae","timestamp":"2026-07-29T04:49:49.074Z","request_id":"req_011CdVkCnwqVZM42TQURX48i"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CdVkCox7G8iggpyF75HAz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You have a few solid options:\n\n1. **p9 wait-for** (the productive-wait skill) — watches a predicate command, notifies when it succeeds/fails, and routes through your configured notify channels. Designed exactly for this. Keeps your terminal clean; you can work on other things.\n\n2. **PushNotification** — direct phone notification from Claude Code. Simpler, but you'd need to hook it to your migration's completion check somehow.\n\n3. **SendMessage to Slack** — if you check Slack on your phone, this is low-friction.\n\n**I'd set up p9.** It's built for blocking operations and has proper failure handling (unlike a dumb timer). The catch is I need to know:\n\n- **How do you check if the migration is done?** (a specific command, log file, database query, API endpoint, or process name?)\n- **Is it already running in the background**, or do you need to kick it off from here before you leave?\n- **What's your preferred notify channel** — phone push, Slack, email, or do you want to configure that?\n\nOnce you give me those, I can wire it up in ~30 seconds. Should be a one-liner like `p9 wait-for staging-migration --cmd 'check-migration-status' --notify push`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6938,"cache_read_input_tokens":17536,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6938},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"REDACTED","uuid":"ae78c178-3b2c-4c9e-98ca-349e619aecc4","timestamp":"2026-07-29T04:49:52.067Z","request_id":"req_011CdVkCnwqVZM42TQURX48i"}
